  </hidden>|<\hidden>
    <mytitle|Wightman axioms (I)>

    \;

    <\myframed>
      <strong|(W0) Relativistic quantum theory>

      Separable Hilbert space <math|\<cal-H\>>; strongly continuous unitary
      representation <math|U> of <math|\<cal-P\><rsup|\<uparrow\>><rsub|+>>;
      <math|U<around|(|a,<with|math-font|Bbb|1>|)>=\<mathe\><rsup|\<mathi\>P\<cdot\>a>>,
      <math|H=P<rsup|0>>.<next-line><em|Spectrum condition:>
      <math|<math-up|spec><around|(|P|)>\<subset\><wide|V|\<bar\>><rsub|<space|-0.17em>+>>,
      so <math|H\<geq\><around|\||<math-bf|P>|\|>\<geq\>0>.<next-line><em|Vacuum:>
      unique (up to phase) unit vector <math|\<Omega\>> with
      <math|U<around|(|a,<with|math-font|Bbb|1>|)>*\<Omega\>=\<Omega\>>.
    </myframed>

    <\myframed>
      <strong|(W1) Fields>

      Dense <math|\<cal-D\>\<ni\>\<Omega\>>; for
      <math|f\<in\>\<cal-S\><around|(|\<bbb-R\><rsup|d>|)>> an operator
      <math|\<varphi\><around|(|f|)>> on <math|\<cal-D\>>,
      <math|\<varphi\><around|(|f|)>*\<cal-D\>\<subset\>\<cal-D\>>,
      <math|U*\<cal-D\>\<subset\>\<cal-D\>>;
      <math|f\<mapsto\><around|\<langle\>|\<chi\>,\<varphi\><around|(|f|)>*\<psi\>|\<rangle\>>>
      tempered; <math|<around|\<langle\>|\<chi\>,\<varphi\><around|(|f|)>*\<psi\>|\<rangle\>>=<around|\<langle\>|\<varphi\><around|(|<wide|f|\<bar\>>|)>*\<chi\>,\<psi\>|\<rangle\>>>.
    </myframed>
  </hidden>|<\hidden>
    <mytitle|Wightman axioms (II)>

    \;

    <\myframed>
      <strong|(W2) Covariance, (W3) Locality, (W4) Cyclicity>

      <math|U<around|(|a,\<Lambda\>|)>*\<varphi\><around|(|f|)>*U<around|(|a,\<Lambda\>|)><rsup|-1>=\<varphi\>*<around|(|f\<circ\><around|(|a,\<Lambda\>|)><rsup|-1>|)>>;<space|1em><math|<around|[|\<varphi\><around|(|f|)>,\<varphi\><around|(|g|)>|]>=0>
      if supports are spacelike separated;<space|1em>polynomials in
      <math|\<varphi\>> applied to <math|\<Omega\>> are dense.
    </myframed>

    Formally <math|\<varphi\><around|(|f|)>=<big|int>\<varphi\><around|(|x|)>*f<around|(|x|)>\<mathd\>x>,
    <math|\<varphi\>*<around|(|x<rsup|0>,<math-bf|x>|)>=\<mathe\><rsup|\<mathi\>H*x<rsup|0>>\<varphi\>*<around|(|0,<math-bf|x>|)>\<mathe\><rsup|-\<mathi\>H*x<rsup|0>>>.

    <with|font-series|bold|Wightman functions>
    <math|W<rsub|n><around|(|f<rsub|1>,\<ldots\>,f<rsub|n>|)>=<around|\<langle\>|\<Omega\>,\<varphi\><around|(|f<rsub|1>|)>*\<cdots\>*\<varphi\><around|(|f<rsub|n>|)>*\<Omega\>|\<rangle\>>\<in\>\<cal-S\><rprime|'><around|(|\<bbb-R\><rsup|d*n>|)>>:

    <\itemize>
      <item>positivity <math|<big|sum><rsub|j,k>W<rsub|j+k>*<around|(|g<rsub|j><rsup|\<ast\>>\<otimes\>g<rsub|k>|)>\<geq\>0>;<space|1em>Poincaré
      invariance;

      <item>spectral condition: Fourier support in
      <math|<wide|V|\<bar\>><rsub|<space|-0.17em>+><rsup|<space|0.17em>n-1>>
      (difference variables);

      <item>locality; cluster property <math|\<Leftrightarrow\>> unique
      vacuum.
    </itemize>
  </hidden>|<\hidden>
    <mytitle|Reconstruction>

    \;

    <\theorem*>
      <dueto|Wightman reconstruction; Streater\UWightman 1964>A sequence
      <math|<around|(|W<rsub|n>|)>> of tempered distributions with
      <math|W<rsub|0>=1> satisfying positivity, invariance, spectral
      condition and locality is the sequence of Wightman functions of a
      Wightman theory, unique up to unitary equivalence.
    </theorem*>

    <\itemize>
      <item>To construct a QFT it suffices to construct its Wightman
      functions.

      <item><strong|Difficulty:> positivity involves all <math|W<rsub|n>> at
      once and refers to real time, while what we can construct lives in
      imaginary time.

      <item>The Euclidean approach replaces it by <strong|reflection
      positivity>, checkable on lattice approximations and stable under
      limits.

      <item>The axioms say nothing about dynamics: no Lagrangian; the
      interaction is hidden in the higher <math|W<rsub|n>>.
    </itemize>
  </hidden>|<\hidden>
    <mytitle|The free field>

    \;

    <math|\<omega\><around|(|<math-bf|p>|)>=<around|(|<around|\||<math-bf|p>|\|><rsup|2>+m<rsup|2>|)><rsup|1/2>>,<space|1em><math|\<mathd\>\<Omega\><rsub|m><around|(|<math-bf|p>|)>=<dfrac|\<mathd\><math-bf|p>|<around|(|2*\<pi\>|)><rsup|s>*<space|0.17em>2*\<omega\><around|(|<math-bf|p>|)>>>
    (invariant measure on <math|H<rsub|m><rsup|+>=<around|{|p<rsup|2>=m<rsup|2>,p<rsup|0>\<gtr\>0|}>>),
    Fock space over <math|L<rsup|2><around|(|\<mathd\>\<Omega\><rsub|m>|)>>:

    <\equation*>
      \<varphi\><around|(|x|)>=<big|int>\<mathd\>\<Omega\><rsub|m><around|(|<math-bf|p>|)>*<around*|[|a<around|(|<math-bf|p>|)>\<mathe\><rsup|-\<mathi\>p\<cdot\>x>+a<rsup|\<ast\>><around|(|<math-bf|p>|)>\<mathe\><rsup|\<mathi\>p\<cdot\>x>|]><rsub|p<rsup|0>=\<omega\><around|(|<math-bf|p>|)>>,
    </equation*>

    with <math|<around|[|a<around|(|<math-bf|p>|)>,a<rsup|\<ast\>><around|(|<math-bf|q>|)>|]>=<around|(|2*\<pi\>|)><rsup|s>*2*\<omega\><around|(|<math-bf|p>|)>*<space|0.17em>\<delta\>*<around|(|<math-bf|p>-<math-bf|q>|)>>,
    <math|a<around|(|<math-bf|p>|)>*\<Omega\>=0>. Then

    <\equation*>
      W<rsub|2>*<around|(|x-y|)>=<big|int>\<mathd\>\<Omega\><rsub|m><around|(|<math-bf|p>|)><space|0.17em>\<mathe\><rsup|-\<mathi\>p\<cdot\><around|(|x-y|)>>,<space|2em><around|\<\|\|\>|\<varphi\><around|(|f|)>*\<Omega\>|\<\|\|\>><rsup|2>=<big|int>\<mathd\>\<Omega\><rsub|m><around|\||<wide|f|~>|\|><rsup|2>\<less\>\<infty\>,
    </equation*>

    but

    <\equation*>
      <around|\<\|\|\>|\<varphi\><around|(|x|)>*\<Omega\>|\<\|\|\>><rsup|2>=W<rsub|2><around|(|0|)>=<big|int>\<mathd\>\<Omega\><rsub|m>=+\<infty\>*<space|2em><around|(|s\<geq\>1|)>.
    </equation*>

    UV divergence: logarithmic for <math|s=1>, power-like for
    <math|s\<geq\>2>. <strong|Not an artefact of the free field.>
  </hidden>|<\hidden>
    <mytitle|No fields at a point>

    \;

    <\proposition*>
      <dueto|Wightman 1964>Assume (W0)\U(W2) and
      <math|\<varphi\><around|(|f|)>*\<Omega\>=<big|int>f<around|(|x|)>*U<around|(|x,<with|math-font|Bbb|1>|)>*\<psi\><space|0.17em>\<mathd\>x>
      for some <math|\<psi\>\<in\>\<cal-H\>>
      (\P<math|\<varphi\><around|(|0|)>*\<Omega\>=\<psi\>> exists\Q). Then
      <math|\<psi\>\<in\>\<bbb-C\>*\<Omega\>>, hence
      <math|\<varphi\><around|(|f|)>*\<Omega\>=c<space|0.17em><around|(|<big|int>f|)>*<space|0.17em>\<Omega\>>.
    </proposition*>

    <\lemma*>
      For <math|d\<geq\>2>, a <em|finite>
      <math|\<cal-L\><rsup|\<uparrow\>><rsub|+>>-invariant measure on
      <math|<wide|V|\<bar\>><rsub|<space|-0.17em>+>> is
      <math|c*<space|0.17em>\<delta\><rsub|0>>.
    </lemma*>

    <\itemize>
      <item>Combined with locality and Reeh\USchlieder: <math|\<varphi\>> is
      a multiple of <math|<with|math-font|Bbb|1>>.

      <item>Quantum fields are <strong|operator-valued distributions>:
      nonlinear expressions in <math|\<varphi\><around|(|x|)>> need a
      definition <math|\<Rightarrow\>> renormalisation.
    </itemize>
  </hidden>|<\hidden>
    <mytitle|Proofs>

    \;

    <with|font-series|bold|Lemma.> A boost of rapidity <math|\<theta\>> acts
    as <math|p<rsup|0>\<pm\>p<rsup|1>\<mapsto\>\<mathe\><rsup|\<pm\>\<theta\>><around|(|p<rsup|0>\<pm\>p<rsup|1>|)>>.
    The sets

    <\equation*>
      S<rsub|j><rsup|\<pm\>>=<around|{|p\<in\><wide|V|\<bar\>><rsub|<space|-0.17em>+>:2<rsup|j>\<leq\>p<rsup|0>\<pm\>p<rsup|1>\<less\>2<rsup|j+1>|}>,<space|2em>j\<in\>\<bbb-Z\>,
    </equation*>

    are mapped to each other by the boost with
    <math|\<mathe\><rsup|\<theta\>>=2>; they are disjoint and cover
    <math|<wide|V|\<bar\>><rsub|<space|-0.17em>+>\<setminus\><around|{|0|}>>.
    Invariance and finiteness force <math|\<mu\><around|(|S<rsup|\<pm\>><rsub|j>|)>=0>.

    <with|font-series|bold|Proposition.>

    <\enumerate>
      <item>Covariance gives <math|<big|int>f<around|(|x|)>*U*<around|(|\<Lambda\>*x|)>*<around*|(|U<around|(|0,\<Lambda\>|)>*\<psi\>-\<psi\>|)>\<mathd\>x=0>
      for all <math|f>, so <math|U<around|(|0,\<Lambda\>|)>*\<psi\>=\<psi\>>.

      <item>The spectral measure <math|\<mu\>> of <math|\<psi\>> for
      translations is finite, supported in
      <math|<wide|V|\<bar\>><rsub|<space|-0.17em>+>> and Lorentz invariant,
      so <math|\<mu\>=<around|\<\|\|\>|\<psi\>|\<\|\|\>><rsup|2>*\<delta\><rsub|0>>.

      <item>Hence <math|U<around|(|a|)>*\<psi\>=\<psi\>> for all <math|a>,
      and <math|\<psi\>\<in\>\<bbb-C\>*\<Omega\>> by uniqueness of the
      vacuum.
    </enumerate>
  </hidden>|<\hidden>
    <mytitle|The Källén\ULehmann representation>

    \;

    Let <math|W<rsub|2><rsup|<around|(|M|)>>> be the free two-point function
    of mass <math|M\<geq\>0> and <math|<around|\<langle\>|\<Omega\>,\<varphi\><around|(|f|)>*\<Omega\>|\<rangle\>>=v*<big|int>f>.

    <\theorem*>
      <dueto|Källén 1952, Lehmann 1954>Under (W0)\U(W2) there is a positive,
      polynomially bounded measure <math|\<rho\>> on
      <math|<around|[|0,\<infty\>|)>> (the <strong|spectral measure> of the
      field) such that

      <\equation*>
        W<rsub|2>*<around|(|x-y|)>=v<rsup|2>+<big|int><rsub|<around|[|0,\<infty\>|)>>\<rho\><around|(|\<mathd\>M<rsup|2>|)>*<space|0.17em>W<rsub|2><rsup|<around|(|M|)>>*<around|(|x-y|)>.
      </equation*>

      (<math|\<rho\><around|(|<around|{|0|}>|)>=0> if <math|d=2>.)
    </theorem*>

    <with|font-series|bold|Sketch.> <math|\<psi\><rsub|f>=\<varphi\><around|(|f|)>*\<Omega\>-v<around|(|<big|int>f|)>*\<Omega\>>
    gives <math|W<rsub|2>-v<rsup|2>> of positive type <math|\<Rightarrow\>>
    (Bochner\USchwartz) Fourier transform of a positive measure
    <math|\<mu\>>, supported in <math|<wide|V|\<bar\>><rsub|<space|-0.17em>+>>,
    <math|\<mu\><around|(|<around|{|0|}>|)>=0>, Lorentz invariant. Orbits are
    the hyperboloids <math|H<rsub|M><rsup|+>> (and the cone for <math|M=0>),
    each with a unique invariant measure <math|\<mathd\>\<Omega\><rsub|M>>.
    Disintegrate along <math|M>.
  </hidden>|<\hidden>
    <mytitle|Reading the spectrum off <math|\<rho\>>>

    \;

    <\itemize>
      <item><strong|Free field:> <math|\<rho\>=\<delta\><rsub|m<rsup|2>>>.
      Conversely <math|\<rho\>=\<delta\><rsub|m<rsup|2>>>, <math|m\<gtr\>0>,
      forces <math|\<varphi\>-v> to be free, by locality (Jost\USchroer).

      <item><strong|Generalised free fields>
      <math|\<varphi\>=<big|sum><rsub|i>c<rsub|i>*\<varphi\><rsub|M<rsub|i>>>
      have <math|\<rho\>=<big|sum><rsub|i>c<rsub|i><rsup|2>*\<delta\><rsub|M<rsub|i><rsup|2>>>
      and no interaction: <math|\<rho\>\<neq\>\<delta\><rsub|m<rsup|2>>> is
      necessary, not sufficient.

      <item><strong|Particles:> an isolated atom
      <math|Z*\<delta\><rsub|m<rsup|2>>> is a particle of mass <math|m>;
      multi-particle continuum from <math|<around|(|2*m|)><rsup|2>> (or
      <math|<around|(|3*m|)><rsup|2>> with
      <math|\<varphi\>\<mapsto\>-\<varphi\>> symmetry). Weakly coupled
      <math|P<around|(|\<varphi\>|)><rsub|2>>: Glimm\UJaffe\USpencer 1974.

      <item><strong|No point fields again:>
      <math|W<rsub|2><rsup|T><around|(|0|)>=<big|int>\<rho\><around|(|\<mathd\>M<rsup|2>|)>*<big|int>\<mathd\>\<Omega\><rsub|M>=\<infty\>>.

      <item><strong|Canonical fields:> CCR at sharp times
      <math|\<Rightarrow\>> <math|<big|int>\<rho\>=1>, so <math|Z\<leq\>1>.
      In <math|d=4> perturbatively <math|<big|int>\<rho\>=\<infty\>>
      (wave-function renormalisation).
    </itemize>
  </hidden>|<\hidden>
    <mytitle|The quantum wave equation>

    \;

    The free field solves, as an operator-valued distribution,

    <\equation*>
      <around|(|\<Box\>+m<rsup|2>|)>*\<varphi\>=0,<space|2em>\<Box\>=\<partial\><rsub|t><rsup|2>-\<Delta\><rsub|<math-bf|x>>,
    </equation*>

    and its sharp-time fields <math|\<varphi\>*<around|(|t,g|)>>,
    <math|\<pi\>*<around|(|t,g|)>>, <math|\<pi\>=\<partial\><rsub|t>*\<varphi\>>,
    satisfy the CCR

    <\equation*>
      <around|[|\<varphi\>*<around|(|t,<math-bf|x>|)>,\<pi\>*<around|(|t,<math-bf|y>|)>|]>=\<mathi\><space|0.17em>\<delta\>*<around|(|<math-bf|x>-<math-bf|y>|)>,<space|2em><around|[|\<varphi\>,\<varphi\>|]>=<around|[|\<pi\>,\<pi\>|]>=0.
    </equation*>

    <\myframed>
      <strong|Picture>

      A <em|linear wave equation with quantum initial data>
      <math|(\<varphi\>*<around|(|0,\<cdot\>|)>,\<pi\>(0,\<cdot\><around|)||)>>,
      \Pdistributed\Q according to the vacuum.
    </myframed>

    Interacting version: <math|<around|(|\<Box\>+m<rsup|2>|)>*\<varphi\>+\<lambda\>*\<varphi\><rsup|3>=0>
    together with the CCR.
  </hidden>|<\hidden>
    <mytitle|The free field on a circle>

    \;

    <math|s=1>, space <math|\<bbb-T\><rsub|L>=\<bbb-R\>/L*\<bbb-Z\>>, momenta
    <math|k\<in\><frac|2*\<pi\>|L>*\<bbb-Z\>>,
    <math|\<omega\><rsub|k>=<around|(|k<rsup|2>+m<rsup|2>|)><rsup|1/2>>:

    <\equation*>
      \<varphi\>*<around|(|0,x|)>=<big|sum><rsub|k><frac|a<rsub|k>\<mathe\><rsup|\<mathi\>k*x>+a<rsub|k><rsup|\<ast\>>\<mathe\><rsup|-\<mathi\>k*x>|<sqrt|2*L*\<omega\><rsub|k>>>,<space|2em><around|[|a<rsub|k>,a<rsup|\<ast\>><rsub|k<rprime|'>>|]>=\<delta\><rsub|k*k<rprime|'>>,<space|2em>H<rsub|0>=<big|sum><rsub|k>\<omega\><rsub|k>*a<rsub|k><rsup|\<ast\>>*a<rsub|k>.
    </equation*>

    <\itemize>
      <item>An infinite family of independent harmonic oscillators, one per
      mode.

      <item>With a UV cutoff <math|<around|\||k|\|>\<leq\>R>:

      <\equation*>
        <around|\<langle\>|\<Omega\>,\<varphi\><rsub|R>*<around|(|0,x|)><rsup|2>*\<Omega\>|\<rangle\>>=<big|sum><rsub|<around|\||k|\|>\<leq\>R><frac|1|2*L*\<omega\><rsub|k>>=<frac|1|2*\<pi\>>*log
        <frac|R|m>+O<around|(|1|)>\<to\>\<infty\>.
      </equation*>

      <item>Wick ordering <math|:\<varphi\><rsub|R><rsup|2>\<assign\>\<varphi\><rsub|R><rsup|2>-<around|\<langle\>|\<Omega\>,\<varphi\><rsub|R><rsup|2>*\<Omega\>|\<rangle\>>>
      removes exactly this divergence (Exercise 1.7).
    </itemize>
  </hidden>|<\hidden>
    <mytitle|Interactions: three problems>

    \;

    <\enumerate>
      <item><strong|Products of distributions.>
      <math|\<varphi\><around|(|x|)><rsup|3>> is meaningless and must be
      renormalised: Wick ordering suffices in <math|d=2>; more counterterms
      in <math|d=3>; triviality in <math|d=4>.

      <item><strong|Haag's theorem.> In infinite volume the interacting field
      at fixed time is not unitarily equivalent to the free one: there is no
      interaction picture.

      <item><strong|Semiboundedness.> Even on <math|\<bbb-T\><rsub|L>>,
      <math|H=H<rsub|0>+\<lambda\>*<big|int>:\<varphi\>*<around|(|0,x|)><rsup|4>:\<mathd\>x>
      is positive plus unbounded below. Nelson 1966: bounded below
      (hypercontractivity). Volume cutoff removed by Glimm\UJaffe; Wightman
      axioms for weak coupling <math|P<around|(|\<varphi\>|)><rsub|2>> by
      Glimm\UJaffe\USpencer 1974.
    </enumerate>

    The Euclidean approach (Symanzik, Nelson, Osterwalder\USchrader,
    Guerra\URosen\USimon) simplifies this enormously.
  </hidden>|<\hidden>
    <vspace*|2.5cm>

    \;

    <with|font-size|1.6|font-series|bold|color|dark red|From real to
    imaginary time>

    <vspace|0.3cm>

    <with|color|dark grey|Lecture 1>

    \;
  </hidden>|<\hidden>
    <mytitle|A lattice Hamiltonian on the circle>

    \;

    Lattice <math|\<Lambda\><rsub|\<varepsilon\>>=\<varepsilon\>*\<bbb-Z\>/L*\<bbb-Z\>>,
    <math|N=L/\<varepsilon\>> sites, <math|\<cal-H\><rsub|\<varepsilon\>>=L<rsup|2>*<around|(|\<bbb-R\><rsup|\<Lambda\><rsub|\<varepsilon\>>>,\<mathd\>\<varphi\>|)>>,
    <math|\<varphi\><rsub|x>> multiplication,
    <math|\<pi\><rsub|x>=-\<mathi\>\<varepsilon\><rsup|-1>*\<partial\><rsub|\<varphi\><rsub|x>>>,
    so <math|<around|[|\<varphi\><rsub|x>,\<pi\><rsub|y>|]>=\<mathi\>\<varepsilon\><rsup|-1>*<with|math-font|Bbb|1><rsub|x=y>>.

    <\equation*>
      H<rsub|\<varepsilon\>>=<big|sum><rsub|x>\<varepsilon\>*<around*|[|<tfrac|1|2>\<pi\><rsub|x><rsup|2>+<tfrac|1|2><around|(|\<nabla\><rsub|\<varepsilon\>>*\<varphi\>|)><rsub|x><rsup|2>+<tfrac|1|2>m<rsup|2>*\<varphi\><rsub|x><rsup|2>+V<around|(|\<varphi\><rsub|x>|)>|]>=-<frac|1|2*\<varepsilon\>>*\<Delta\><rsub|\<bbb-R\><rsup|N>>+U<rsub|\<varepsilon\>><around|(|\<varphi\>|)>.
    </equation*>

    <\itemize>
      <item>Heisenberg fields solve the <strong|lattice wave equation>

      <\equation*>
        \<partial\><rsub|t><rsup|2>*\<varphi\><rsub|x>=<around|(|\<Delta\><rsub|\<varepsilon\>>*\<varphi\>|)><rsub|x>-m<rsup|2>*\<varphi\><rsub|x>-V<rprime|'><around|(|\<varphi\><rsub|x>|)>
      </equation*>

      \V the quantum wave equation, now rigorous.

      <item>Schrödinger operator with confining potential: self-adjoint,
      compact resolvent, <math|\<mathe\><rsup|-t*H<rsub|\<varepsilon\>>>>
      trace class with positive kernel.

      <item>Perron\UFrobenius: simple ground state
      <math|\<Omega\><rsub|\<varepsilon\>>\<gtr\>0>, energy
      <math|E<rsub|0>>.<space|1em> <math|<wide|H|\<bar\>>\<assign\>H<rsub|\<varepsilon\>>-E<rsub|0>\<geq\>0>.
    </itemize>
  </hidden>|<\hidden>
    <mytitle|Positivity of the energy <math|\<Rightarrow\>> Wick rotation>

    \;

    <wide-tabular|<tformat|<cwith|1|1|1|-1|cell-valign|t>|<cwith|1|1|1|-1|cell-hyphen|t>|<cwith|1|1|1|-1|cell-lsep|0em>|<cwith|1|1|1|-1|cell-rsep|1em>|<cwith|1|1|1|1|cell-width|0.6par>|<cwith|1|1|1|1|cell-hmode|exact>|<cwith|1|1|2|2|cell-width|0.36par>|<cwith|1|1|2|2|cell-hmode|exact>|<table|<row|<\cell>
      For bounded <math|F<rsub|j>> and <math|F<rsub|j><around|(|t|)>=\<mathe\><rsup|\<mathi\>t*H>F<rsub|j>\<mathe\><rsup|-\<mathi\>t*H>>:

      <\equation*>
        W<around|(|t<rsub|1>,\<ldots\>,t<rsub|n>|)>=<around|\<langle\>|\<Omega\><rsub|\<varepsilon\>>,F<rsub|1>\<mathe\><rsup|-\<mathi\><around|(|t<rsub|1>-t<rsub|2>|)>*<wide|H|\<bar\>>>F<rsub|2>*\<cdots\>*F<rsub|n>*\<Omega\><rsub|\<varepsilon\>>|\<rangle\>>.
      </equation*>

      <\proposition*>
        <math|W> extends analytically to <math|<math-up|Im><around|(|t<rsub|j>-t<rsub|j+1>|)>\<less\>0>.
        At <math|t<rsub|j>=-\<mathi\>\<tau\><rsub|j>>,
        <math|\<tau\><rsub|1>\<geq\>\<ldots\>\<geq\>\<tau\><rsub|n>>, it
        gives the <strong|Schwinger functions>

        <\equation*>
          S<around|(|\<tau\><rsub|1>,\<ldots\>,\<tau\><rsub|n>|)>=<around|\<langle\>|\<Omega\><rsub|\<varepsilon\>>,F<rsub|1>\<mathe\><rsup|-<around|(|\<tau\><rsub|1>-\<tau\><rsub|2>|)>*<wide|H|\<bar\>>>F<rsub|2>*\<cdots\>*F<rsub|n>*\<Omega\><rsub|\<varepsilon\>>|\<rangle\>>,
        </equation*>

        which determine <math|W>.
      </proposition*>
    </cell>|<\cell>
