    Rows are quantum configurations at fixed imaginary time; the transfer
    matrix connects consecutive rows. As <math|T\<to\>\<infty\>>, the rows
    form a stationary Markov process whose one-time marginal is
    <math|\<Omega\><rsub|\<varepsilon\>><around|(|\<varphi\>|)><rsup|2>\<mathd\>\<varphi\>>.
  </hidden>|<\hidden>
    <mytitle|Classical statistical mechanics>

    \;

    Isotropic lattice <math|\<delta\>=\<varepsilon\>>:

    <\equation*>
      S<rsub|\<varepsilon\>><around|(|\<varphi\>|)>=<big|sum><rsub|<around|\<langle\>|u,v|\<rangle\>>><tfrac|1|2><around|(|\<varphi\><rsub|u>-\<varphi\><rsub|v>|)><rsup|2>+\<varepsilon\><rsup|2>*<big|sum><rsub|u><around*|[|<tfrac|1|2>m<rsup|2>*\<varphi\><rsub|u><rsup|2>+V<around|(|\<varphi\><rsub|u>|)>|]>.
    </equation*>

    <\itemize>
      <item><math|\<mu\><rsub|\<varepsilon\>>\<propto\><big|prod><rsub|<around|\<langle\>|u,v|\<rangle\>>>\<mathe\><rsup|-<frac|1|2>*<around|(|\<varphi\><rsub|u>-\<varphi\><rsub|v>|)><rsup|2>><big|prod><rsub|u>\<nu\><rsub|\<varepsilon\>><around|(|\<mathd\>\<varphi\><rsub|u>|)>>,
      <space|1em> <math|\<nu\><rsub|\<varepsilon\>><around|(|\<mathd\>a|)>=\<mathe\><rsup|-\<varepsilon\><rsup|2>*<around|(|<frac|1|2>*m<rsup|2>*a<rsup|2>+V<around|(|a|)>|)>>\<mathd\>a>.

      <item>A <strong|ferromagnetic nearest-neighbour spin system> with
      unbounded spins: short-range classical statistical mechanics.

      <item>In dimension <math|d>: <math|\<varepsilon\><rsup|d-2>*<big|sum><rsub|<around|\<langle\>|u,v|\<rangle\>>>>
      and <math|\<varepsilon\><rsup|d>*<big|sum><rsub|u>>.

      <item>Nearest-neighbour <math|\<Rightarrow\>> <strong|reflection
      positive>: the Euclidean shadow of <math|\<mathe\><rsup|-\<varepsilon\>*H>\<geq\>0>.
      Conversely, RP <math|\<Rightarrow\>> Hilbert space and <math|H\<geq\>0>
      (Exercises 2.5, 2.7).
    </itemize>
  </hidden>|<\hidden>
    <mytitle|A dictionary>

    \;

    <tabular*|<tformat|<cwith|1|-1|1|-1|cell-valign|c>|<cwith|1|1|1|-1|cell-tborder|1ln>|<cwith|1|1|1|-1|cell-bborder|1ln>|<cwith|8|8|1|-1|cell-bborder|1ln>|<table|<row|<cell|Quantum
    (real time)>|<cell|Euclidean field theory>|<cell|Statistical
    mechanics>>|<row|<cell|Hilbert space positivity,
    <math|H\<geq\>0>>|<cell|reflection positivity>|<cell|RP of n.n.
