    temperature <math|\<beta\>>>|<cell|length of the time
    circle>|<cell|\V>>|<row|<cell|mass gap
    <math|E<rsub|1>-E<rsub|0>>>|<cell|exponential decay>|<cell|inverse
    correlation length>>|<row|<cell|continuum limit>|<cell|UV cutoff
    <math|\<varepsilon\>\<to\>0>>|<cell|critical point, scaling
    limit>>|<row|<cell|renormalisation>|<cell|counterterms>|<cell|tuning to
    criticality>>>>>
  </hidden>|<\hidden>
    <mytitle|Continuum limit <math|=> critical point>

    \;

    <\itemize>
      <item>In lattice units the mass is <math|\<varepsilon\>*m\<to\>0>:
      correlation length <math|\<xi\>\<approx\><around|(|\<varepsilon\>*m|)><rsup|-1>\<to\>\<infty\>>
      lattice spacings.

      <item>Continuum QFT <math|=> <strong|scaling limit of short-range spin
      systems approaching criticality> (Wilson). Conversely, RP critical
      models with nontrivial scaling limits give candidate QFTs.

      <item>Griffiths\USimon: <math|\<varphi\><rsup|4>> spins as limits of
      normalised sums of ferromagnetically coupled Ising spins; critical 4D
      Ising and <math|\<varphi\><rsup|4><rsub|4>> have Gaussian scaling
      limits (ADC 2021).
    </itemize>

    <\myframed>
      <strong|Renormalisation already appears>

      For <math|V=\<lambda\>*a<rsup|4>> and fixed
      <math|<around|(|m,\<lambda\>|)>> the limit is trivial:
      <math|c<rsub|\<varepsilon\>>=\<bbb-E\><around|[|\<varphi\><rsub|u><rsup|2>|]>=<frac|1|2*\<pi\>>*log
      <frac|1|\<varepsilon\>*m>+O<around|(|1|)>\<to\>\<infty\>>. Take
      <math|V<rsub|\<varepsilon\>><around|(|a|)>=\<lambda\>*<around|(|a<rsup|4>-6*c<rsub|\<varepsilon\>>*a<rsup|2>|)>>,
      i.e. <math|\<lambda\>:a<rsup|4>>: up to a constant. Enough in
      <math|d=2>; not in <math|d=3>.
    </myframed>
  </hidden>|<\hidden>
    <mytitle|Path integrals>

    \;

    Formally, as <math|\<varepsilon\>\<to\>0> and <math|L,T\<to\>\<infty\>>:

    <\equation*>
      \<mu\><around|(|\<mathd\>\<varphi\>|)>*`*`="*Z<rsup|-1>*exp
      <around*|(|-<big|int><rsub|\<bbb-R\><rsup|d>><around*|[|<tfrac|1|2>\|\<nabla\>*\<varphi\>\|<rsup|2>+<tfrac|1|2>m<rsup|2>*\<varphi\><rsup|2>+V<around|(|\<varphi\>|)>|]>\<mathd\>x|)>*\<cal-D\>*\<varphi\>.
    </equation*>

    <\itemize>
      <item>Neither <math|\<cal-D\>*\<varphi\>> nor the action make sense:
      typical <math|\<varphi\>> are distributions.

      <item>The Gaussian part defines the <strong|Gaussian free field>
      <math|\<mu\><rsub|m>> (next lecture).

      <item>Then <math|\<mu\>\<propto\>\<mathe\><rsup|-<big|int>V<rsub|<math-up|ren>><around|(|\<varphi\>|)>>\<mu\><rsub|m>>:
      meaningful in finite volume for <math|d=2> (and, with more work,
      <math|d=3>).
    </itemize>

    <with|font-series|bold|Question.> Which measures on
    <math|\<cal-S\><rprime|'><around|(|\<bbb-R\><rsup|d>|)>> correspond to
    relativistic QFTs?
  </hidden>|<\shown>
    <mytitle|Osterwalder\USchrader axioms>

    \;

    <math|<wide|\<mu\>|^><around|(|f|)>=<big|int>\<mathe\><rsup|\<mathi\>\<varphi\><around|(|f|)>>\<mu\><around|(|\<mathd\>\<varphi\>|)>>,<space|1em><math|\<Theta\>*<around|(|\<tau\>,<math-bf|x>|)>=<around|(|-\<tau\>,<math-bf|x>|)>>.

    <\description>
      <item*|OS0><em|Analyticity:> <math|z\<mapsto\><wide|\<mu\>|^><around|(|<big|sum><rsub|j>z<rsub|j>*f<rsub|j>|)>>
      entire.

      <item*|OS1><em|Regularity:> <math|<around|\||<wide|\<mu\>|^><around|(|f|)>|\|>\<leq\>exp
      <around*|(|c*<around|(|<around|\<\|\|\>|f|\<\|\|\>><rsub|L<rsup|1>>+<around|\<\|\|\>|f|\<\|\|\>><rsup|p><rsub|L<rsup|p>>|)>|)>>,
      <math|p\<in\><around|[|1,2|]>>, complex <math|f>.

      <item*|OS2><em|Euclidean invariance.>

      <item*|OS3><em|Reflection positivity:> for real <math|f<rsub|i>>
      supported in <math|<around|{|\<tau\>\<gtr\>0|}>>,
      <math|<around*|(|<wide|\<mu\>|^>*<around|(|f<rsub|i>-\<Theta\>*f<rsub|j>|)>|)><rsub|i*j>\<geq\>0>.

      <item*|OS4><em|Ergodicity> under time translations.
    </description>

    <\theorem*>
      <dueto|Osterwalder\USchrader 1973/75>OS0\UOS3 <math|\<Rightarrow\>> the
      moments of <math|\<mu\>> are the Schwinger functions of a unique
      Wightman theory; OS4 <math|\<Leftrightarrow\>> unique vacuum.
    </theorem*>
  </shown>|<\hidden>
    <mytitle|Reconstruction: the idea>

    \;

    <\itemize>
      <item><math|\<cal-E\><rsub|+>=> functions of
      <math|\<varphi\>\|<rsub|<around|{|\<tau\>\<gtr\>0|}>>>, with
      <math|<around|(|F,G|)>=\<bbb-E\><rsub|\<mu\>><around|[|<wide|\<Theta\>*F|\<bar\>><space|0.17em>G|]>\<geq\>0>
      by OS3.

      <item>Quotient by null vectors and complete: physical Hilbert space
      <math|\<cal-H\>>.

      <item>Time translations by <math|t\<geq\>0> preserve
      <math|\<cal-E\><rsub|+>> and descend to a self-adjoint contraction
      semigroup <math|\<mathe\><rsup|-t*H>>: <strong|positivity of the energy
      is recovered from reflection positivity>.

      <item>Vacuum <math|=> class of <math|1>; analytic continuation
      <math|\<tau\>\<to\>\<mathi\>t> gives the Wightman functions.
    </itemize>

    <\myframed>
      <strong|The Euclidean strategy>

      (1) regularise (lattice, torus); (2) renormalise; (3) uniform
      estimates, remove cutoffs; (4) verify OS axioms (RP survives limits,
      Euclidean invariance recovered, regularity, clustering); (5) prove
      non-Gaussianity.
    </myframed>
  </hidden>|<\hidden>
    <mytitle|Exercises and reading>

    \;

    <wide-tabular|<tformat|<cwith|1|1|1|-1|cell-valign|t>|<cwith|1|1|1|-1|cell-hyphen|t>|<cwith|1|1|1|-1|cell-lsep|0em>|<cwith|1|1|1|-1|cell-rsep|1em>|<cwith|1|1|1|1|cell-width|0.5par>|<cwith|1|1|1|1|cell-hmode|exact>|<cwith|1|1|2|2|cell-width|0.46par>|<cwith|1|1|2|2|cell-hmode|exact>|<table|<row|<\cell>
      <with|font-series|bold|Exercises> (numbering of the notes)

      <\itemize>
        <item>1.3 Which restrictions of the free field make sense?

        <item>1.5\U1.6 Canonical sum rule; generalised free fields.

        <item>2.2 Harmonic oscillator and Ornstein\UUhlenbeck.

        <item>2.4 Correlation length and criticality.

        <item>2.5, 2.7 Reflection positivity on the lattice; toy OS
        reconstruction.
      </itemize>
    </cell>|<\cell>
      <with|font-series|bold|Reading>

      <\itemize>
        <item>Streater\UWightman, <em|PCT, Spin and Statistics, and All
